# Design analysis for the D5/3 + D11/1 fused variant
# a) Concrete behavior and trace:
#    The rare 3x3 cell still acts as a binary stencil, and a strict subset of its active sites is still
#    shown as minority anchors. The large change is what lies underneath the 7x7 cell field: instead of
#    one repeated majority tile, every absolute (row mod 3, col mod 3) position carries its own 2-color
#    template with a single accent pixel. After locating the 3x3 stencil:
#    - Original task: every active enlarged cell becomes the same minority tile.
#    - D11 alone: every active enlarged cell reveals the template belonging to that absolute position.
